assignee: unbraind
author: codex-root
estimated_minutes: 480
acceptance_criteria: "Built hassio exposes typed bounded repairs list/detail, explicit ignore/unignore, and admin fix-flow start/read/submit operations; Built hassio exposes typed search/related topology with every current Home Assistant item type, deterministic normalized output, count and per-type bounds; Mutating repairs operations respect HASSIO_READONLY and require explicit confirmation where appropriate; Every command and global flag has detailed help and schema/documentation coverage across all supported formats; Exact 100/100/100/100 source coverage, 100 percent docstrings, file-size, duplication, static, PM, security, package, release-dry-run, setup wizard, and privacy-safe live gates pass"
definition_of_ready: "Core 2026.8.0 tagged source, current official docs, live 2026.7.4 structural behavior, complete PM history and graph, GitHub duplicates, repository source, dependency types, baseline coverage, and private settings health inspected"
goal: complete-agent-home-assistant-interface
objective: typed-repairs-and-topology-diagnostics
value: Let agents understand configuration problems and dependency blast radius without raw WebSocket payload construction or broad inventory downloads.
impact: "Improves safe diagnosis, remediation planning, token efficiency, and programmatic automation across Home Assistant resources."
outcome: Production-ready typed diagnostic and repair workflows merged with exact-head evidence and no unresolved review findings.
why_now: Core 2026.8.0 is current and these durable built-in contracts remain available only through generic passthrough in the CLI.
